# vdbleafpoints

- Label: VDB Leaf Points
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbleafpoints.html
- Summary (EN): Creates one point for each active leaf of an incoming VDB, where a leaf is an 8x8x8 block of voxels. The points map one-to-one to the VDB topology and can feed geometry-based operations.
- Résumé (FR) : Crée un point par feuille active d'un VDB (bloc de 8 × 8 × 8 voxels), ce qui permet d'utiliser la topologie dans des opérations géométriques.

- Inputs meaning: ["vdb: the VDB whose active leaves each generate a point"]

- Key parameters: ["Set Positions: sets each point's P to the centre voxel of its leaf", "Point Attributes: adds extra attributes for later OpenCL nodes. Name; Class (only Detail and Point apply to points); Type (integer or float); Tuple Size"]

- Caveats: ["Leaf order within a VDB is not deterministic, so the order of output points should not be relied upon"]

